<title>GERMANY: Vedrine says France wants to keep euro timetable.</title>
<headline>Vedrine says France wants to keep euro timetable.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>French Foreign Minister Hubert Vedrine said at a news conference in Bonn with German Foreign Minister Klaus Kinkel that France wants to maintain the timetable for the launch of the single European currency.</p>
<p>&quot;We want to keep the timetable for the euro's introduction,&quot; Vedrine told the news conference.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom 49 228 260 97160</p>
</text>
